Robin Janvrin, played by Roger Allam.

10
00:46:49,090 --> 00:46:55,090
The Queen is a 2006 docudrama film directed by Stephen
Frears and written by Peter Morgan.

11
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
The film depicts the death of Diana, Princess of Wales in 1997.

12
00:56:10,909 --> 00:56:16,909
The royal family regards Diana's death as a private affair and thus not to be treated as an official royal death, in contrast with the views of Prime
Minister Tony Blair and Diana's ex-husband, Prince Charles, who favour the general public's desire for an official expression of grief.

13
01:00:51,818 --> 01:00:57,818
Matters are further complicated by the media, royal protocol regarding
Diana's official status, and wider issues about republicanism.

14
01:05:32,727 --> 01:05:38,727
The film's development coincided with a revival of favourable public sentiment in respect to the British
monarchy, a downturn in fortunes for Blair, and the inquest into Diana's death, Operation Paget.

15
01:10:13,636 --> 01:10:19,636
Michael Sheen reprised his role as Blair from The Deal.

16
01:14:54,545 --> 01:15:00,545
He would play Blair again in The Special Relationship.

17
01:19:35,454 --> 01:19:41,454
The Queen garnered widespread critical and popular acclaim for Helen
Mirren playing the title role of Queen Elizabeth II.

18
01:24:16,363 --> 01:24:22,363
Mirren was praised by the Queen herself and was
invited to dinner at Buckingham Palace.

19
01:28:57,272 --> 01:29:03,272
However, Mirren declined to attend due to filming commitments in Hollywood.

20
01:33:38,181 --> 01:33:44,181
The film explores themes of dying and death, great britain,
upper class, loss of loved one, sadness.

21
01:38:19,090 --> 01:38:25,090
The tone is emotional.
